                <head>C.</head>
                <note rend="inline">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Williams to United States consuls in China,</hi>
                </note>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-07-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 17, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: His Excellency Hon. Anson Burlingame,
                    United States minister, having been in consultation with his imperial highness
                    Prince Kung, respecting the penalty to be levied on the masters of merchant
                    vessels under the treaty of Tientsin for overpassing the allotted time of 48
                    hours after entering port without reporting their arrival, it has been agreed
                    between them that pending a reference to Washington, the XlXth article of said
                    treaty shall be understood to include <hi rendition="#italic">hulks</hi> and
                    storeships of every kind, under the designation of <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >merchant vessels,</hi> and shall be defined for this offence by the first
                    sentence of article XXXVII of the British treaty, and the legal penalty to be
                    inflicted on the master for neglecting to report his arrival within 48 hours
                    shall be a fine of 50 taels for every day’s delay, but not to exceed in all the
                    sum of 200 taels.</p>
                <p>I am directed to make known this modification of article XIX of the American
                    treaty for your guidance and the information of American citizens under your
                    jurisdiction.</p>
                <p>By order:</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S. WELLS WILLIAMS, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of
                        Legation,</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>To——— ———, <hi rendition="#italic">United States Consul</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
